OL,3,GNEWSA'My abuser could be released early
OL,4,A- it's sheer terror'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA woman whose ex-partner was jailed for
OL,7,Fattacking and controlling her has
OL,8,Fwarned "there will be a death" if
OL,9,Fdomestic abusers are released from
OL,10,Fprison early.
OL,12,FHelen Duncanson from North Yorkshire
OL,13,Fhas said she is suffering from "night
OL,14,Fterrors and panic" after being told her
OL,15,Fabuser could be eligible for early
OL,16,Frelease.
OL,18,FIn January, Michael Boyes, 40, was
OL,19,Fsentenced to three and a half years in
OL,20,Fprison but Helen has been told he could
OL,21,Fbe freed in March 2027 after serving
OL,22,Fonly 14 months.
OL,23,APub: 01-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,388,380,200,160,0,100
